\subsection{Statistical analysis}
We compare IGD vs CoT at matched budgets via Welch’s unequal-variance t-test and report Hedges’ $g$ effect size with small-sample correction and Benjamini--Hochberg (BH) control of the false discovery rate:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em, itemsep=0.2em]
\item Welch’s $t = \dfrac{\bar{x}_1-\bar{x}_2}{\sqrt{s_1^2/n_1+s_2^2/n_2}}$ with Satterthwaite degrees of freedom,
\item Hedges’ $g = J\!\left(1-\dfrac{3}{4(n_1+n_2)-9}\right)\dfrac{\bar{x}_1-\bar{x}_2}{s_p}$ with pooled SD $s_p$,
\item BH: sort p-values $p_{(k)}$, find largest $k$ with $p_{(k)} \le \alpha k/m$, reject all $p_{(i)}$ with $i\le k$ at $\alpha{=}0.05$.
\end{itemize}
