\section{Complexity and performance analysis}
We analyze the token-level and asymptotic costs of core algorithms.

\subsection{Asymptotic considerations}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em, itemsep=0.2em]
\item IGD: Maintaining $m$ threads with incremental posteriors yields per-decision overhead $O(m)$ for index evaluation and $O(1)$ for advancing the chosen thread, plus token generation cost for the LLM micro-action. With appropriate data structures, amortized updates to uncertainty proxies remain $O(1)$ per thread.
